## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to extend behavior at runtime using design patterns while ensuring safety and observability in a large-scale system.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern
- Registry / plugin architecture
- Hot-reload safe updates
- Observability for experiments
- Performance considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Interfaces and registry core
type Context = { region: string; userId: string; device: string; time: number };
interface Strategy { evaluate(ctx: Context): string }
class Registry {
  private map = new Map<string, Strategy>();
  register(name: string, impl: Strategy) { this.map.set(name, impl); }
  get(name: string) { return this.map.get(name); }
}
```

```javascript
// Usage sketch
const registry = new Registry();
registry.register('region', new RegionStrategy());
registry.register('multivariate', new MultiVarStrategy());

function evaluateFlag(flag, ctx) {
  const stratName = flag.strategy; // chosen at runtime
  const strat = registry.get(stratName);
  return strat.evaluate(ctx);
}
```

