## Why This Is Asked
High-throughput gateways must support evolving protocols without touching core logic. A pluggable adapter layer provides clean separation and runtime extensibility.

## Key Concepts
- Adapter pattern for protocol translation
- Runtime registry for plugin adapters
- Low-allocation, fast dispatch to appropriate adapter
- Clear interfaces to avoid gateway coupling

## Code Example
```javascript
interface ProtocolAdapter {
  canHandle(req: Request): boolean;
  translate(req: Request): InternalRequest;
}
class ProtocolRegistry {
  private map = new Map<string, ProtocolAdapter>();
  register(name: string, a: ProtocolAdapter): void { this.map.set(name, a); }
  translate(req: Request): InternalRequest {
    const a = this.map.get(req.protocol);
    if (!a) throw new Error('Unsupported protocol');
    return a.translate(req);
  }
}
```

